` or `POST /scenes/{scene_id}/plan/reject`. However, the guidance suggests I should keep scene-edit operations separate from dedicated command endpoints, since the `/plan` command should return canonical operations along with an apply token. The client can only accept or reject previewed plans, which means a server reject endpoint isn't necessary. I'll just note that previews expire if not used.\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ilha31U1APCYBINHoLrvKqJw|fc_0e754b82ab019da10169e1d365d2048193acf560926951099f","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"docs/mvp_duet.md","edits":[{"oldText":"* Typed edit operations:\n\n  * `move_object`\n  * `rotate_object`\n  * `replace_object`\n  * `add_object`\n  * `remove_object`\n  * `lock_entity`\n  * `unlock_entity`\n  * `repaint_surface`\n  * `swap_flooring`\n  * `generate_photoreal`\n  * `undo_last_change`\n* Five hard constraints\n","newText":"* Typed scene-edit operations:\n\n  * `move_object`\n  * `rotate_object`\n  * `replace_object`\n  * `add_object`\n  * `remove_object`\n  * `lock_entity`\n  * `unlock_entity`\n  * `repaint_surface`\n  * `swap_flooring`\n* Dedicated command endpoints for:\n\n  * `generate_photoreal`\n  * `undo_last_change`\n* Five hard constraints\n"},{"oldText":"### 7.1 Capture flow\n\n1. User opens iOS companion app.\n2. User scans a bedroom with RoomPlan.\n3. App serializes RoomPlan output into capture payload.\n4. App uploads:\n\n   * RoomPlan scene payload\n   * metadata\n   * optional raw video for splat training\n5. Backend creates canonical scene and returns `scene_id`.\n6. User opens web editor on laptop with that `scene_id`.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n* A valid RoomPlan scan produces a canonical scene without manual intervention.\n* Scene becomes editable before splat is ready.\n* If splat never completes, the editor still functions.\n\n### 7.2 Editor load flow\n\n1. Web app loads scene JSON.\n2. Scan pane shows RoomPlan parametric preview.\n3. Layout pane shows top-down shell, openings, and object OBBs.\n4. Render pane shows Quick render using retrieved assets.\n5. If splat later becomes ready, scan pane updates without changing scene state.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n* Editor loads a usable scene from canonical JSON only.\n* Scan pane is read-only and never used for validation or mutation.\n* Quick render and layout always reflect current committed scene version.\n\n### 7.3 Edit flow\n\n1. User selects an object/surface or types in chat.\n2. LLM planner converts prompt into an operation plan.\n3. Validator simulates the plan on a scene copy.\n4. If valid, backend commits the plan atomically.\n5. UI updates layout and quick render.\n6. If invalid, UI shows a reason and optional suggested next action.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n* One user prompt results in either:\n\n  * one atomic committed plan, or\n  * one clarification request, or\n  * one rejection with reason code\n* No partial commit on failed plan validation.\n","newText":"### 7.1 Capture flow\n\n1. User opens iOS companion app.\n2. User scans a bedroom with RoomPlan.\n3. App serializes RoomPlan output into capture payload.\n4. App uploads:\n\n   * RoomPlan scene payload\n   * metadata\n   * optional raw video for splat training\n5. Backend creates the canonical scene, issues a short-lived one-time handoff grant, and returns:\n\n   * `scene_id`\n   * `handoff_url`\n   * QR payload encoding the same one-time grant\n   * `expires_at`\n6. User opens the web editor on a laptop by redeeming the handoff URL or QR payload into an authenticated web session scoped to that `scene_id`.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n* A valid RoomPlan scan produces a canonical scene and a private handoff grant without manual intervention.\n* Raw `scene_id` possession alone is insufficient to open the web editor in MVP.\n* Handoff grants are short-lived, one-time use, and scene-scoped.\n* Scene becomes editable before splat is ready.\n* If splat never completes, the editor still functions.\n\n### 7.2 Editor load flow\n\n1. Web app redeems a valid handoff grant, or resumes an authenticated scene-scoped session, and requests the current scene read model.\n2. Scan pane shows RoomPlan parametric preview.\n3. Layout pane shows top-down shell, openings, and object OBBs.\n4. Render pane shows Quick render using retrieved assets.\n5. If splat later becomes ready, scan pane updates without changing scene state.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n* Editor access requires an authenticated session scoped to the scene; there are no public scene URLs in MVP.\n* Editor loads a usable scene from canonical JSON only.\n* Scan pane is read-only and never used for validation or mutation.\n* Quick render and layout always reflect current committed scene version.\n\n### 7.3 Edit flow\n\n1. User selects an object/surface or types in chat.\n2. Backend planning resolves the request into one of:\n\n   * a clarification request\n   * a rejection with reason code\n   * a canonical scene-edit plan preview with server-issued apply credentials\n   * a dedicated command request (`photoreal` or `undo`) routed to its own endpoint\n3. For scene-edit previews, the client may only accept or abandon the preview; it may not edit the returned ops.\n4. If the user accepts a valid scene-edit preview before expiry, backend validates against the current head and commits atomically.\n5. UI updates layout and quick render.\n6. If invalid or stale, UI shows a reason and optional suggested next action.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n* One user prompt results in either:\n\n  * one atomic committed plan, or\n  * one clarification request, or\n  * one rejection with reason code, or\n  * one dedicated command execution routed through its own endpoint\n* No partial commit on failed plan validation.\n* The client never submits user-edited ops for apply.\n"}]},"partialJson":"{\"path\":\"docs/mvp_duet.md\",\"edits\":[{\"oldText\":\"* Typed edit operations:\\n\\n  * `move_object`\\n  * `rotate_object`\\n  * `replace_object`\\n  * `add_object`\\n  * `remove_object`\\n  * `lock_entity`\\n  * `unlock_entity`\\n  * `repaint_surface`\\n  * `swap_flooring`\\n  * `generate_photoreal`\\n  * `undo_last_change`\\n* Five hard constraints\\n\",\"newText\":\"* Typed scene-edit operations:\\n\\n  * `move_object`\\n  * `rotate_object`\\n  * `replace_object`\\n  * `add_object`\\n  * `remove_object`\\n  * `lock_entity`\\n  * `unlock_entity`\\n  * `repaint_surface`\\n  * `swap_flooring`\\n* Dedicated command endpoints for:\\n\\n  * `generate_photoreal`\\n  * `undo_last_change`\\n* Five hard constraints\\n\"},{\"oldText\":\"### 7.1 Capture flow\\n\\n1. User opens iOS companion app.\\n2. User scans a bedroom with RoomPlan.\\n3. App serializes RoomPlan output into capture payload.\\n4. App uploads:\\n\\n   * RoomPlan scene payload\\n   * metadata\\n   * optional raw video for splat training\\n5. Backend creates canonical scene and returns `scene_id`.\\n6. User opens web editor on laptop with that `scene_id`.\\n\\n**Acceptance criteria**\\n\\n* A valid RoomPlan scan produces a canonical scene without manual intervention.\\n* Scene becomes editable before splat is ready.\\n* If splat never completes, the editor still functions.\\n\\n### 7.2 Editor load flow\\n\\n1. Web app loads scene JSON.\\n2. Scan pane shows RoomPlan parametric preview.\\n3. Layout pane shows top-down shell, openings, and object OBBs.\\n4. Render pane shows Quick render using retrieved assets.\\n5. If splat later becomes ready, scan pane updates without changing scene state.\\n\\n**Acceptance criteria**\\n\\n* Editor loads a usable scene from canonical JSON only.\\n* Scan pane is read-only and never used for validation or mutation.\\n* Quick render and layout always reflect current committed scene version.\\n\\n### 7.3 Edit flow\\n\\n1. User selects an object/surface or types in chat.\\n2. LLM planner converts prompt into an operation plan.\\n3. Validator simulates the plan on a scene copy.\\n4. If valid, backend commits the plan atomically.\\n5. UI updates layout and quick render.\\n6. If invalid, UI shows a reason and optional suggested next action.\\n\\n**Acceptance criteria**\\n\\n* One user prompt results in either:\\n\\n  * one atomic committed plan, or\\n  * one clarification request, or\\n  * one rejection with reason code\\n* No partial commit on failed plan validation.\\n\",\"newText\":\"### 7.1 Capture flow\\n\\n1. User opens iOS companion app.\\n2. User scans a bedroom with RoomPlan.\\n3. App serializes RoomPlan output into capture payload.\\n4. App uploads:\\n\\n   * RoomPlan scene payload\\n   * metadata\\n   * optional raw video for splat training\\n5. Backend creates the canonical scene, issues a short-lived one-time handoff grant, and returns:\\n\\n   * `scene_id`\\n   * `handoff_url`\\n   * QR payload encoding the same one-time grant\\n   * `expires_at`\\n6. User opens the web editor on a laptop by redeeming the handoff URL or QR payload into an authenticated web session scoped to that `scene_id`.\\n\\n**Acceptance criteria**\\n\\n* A valid RoomPlan scan produces a canonical scene and a private handoff grant without manual intervention.\\n* Raw `scene_id` possession alone is insufficient to open the web editor in MVP.\\n* Handoff grants are short-lived, one-time use, and scene-scoped.\\n* Scene becomes editable before splat is ready.\\n* If splat never completes, the editor still functions.\\n\\n### 7.2 Editor load flow\\n\\n1. Web app redeems a valid handoff grant, or resumes an authenticated scene-scoped session, and requests the current scene read model.\\n2. Scan pane shows RoomPlan parametric preview.\\n3. Layout pane shows top-down shell, openings, and object OBBs.\\n4. Render pane shows Quick render using retrieved assets.\\n5. If splat later becomes ready, scan pane updates without changing scene state.\\n\\n**Acceptance criteria**\\n\\n* Editor access requires an authenticated session scoped to the scene; there are no public scene URLs in MVP.\\n* Editor loads a usable scene from canonical JSON only.\\n* Scan pane is read-only and never used for validation or mutation.\\n* Quick render and layout always reflect current committed scene version.\\n\\n### 7.3 Edit flow\\n\\n1. User selects an object/surface or types in chat.\\n2. Backend planning resolves the request into one of:\\n\\n   * a clarification request\\n   * a rejection with reason code\\n   * a canonical scene-edit plan preview with server-issued apply credentials\\n   * a dedicated command request (`photoreal` or `undo`) routed to its own endpoint\\n3. For scene-edit previews, the client may only accept or abandon the preview; it may not edit the returned ops.\\n4. If the user accepts a valid scene-edit preview before expiry, backend validates against the current head and commits atomically.\\n5. UI updates layout and quick render.\\n6. If invalid or stale, UI shows a reason and optional suggested next action.\\n\\n**Acceptance criteria**\\n\\n* One user prompt results in either:\\n\\n  * one atomic committed plan, or\\n  * one clarification request, or\\n  * one rejection with reason code, or\\n  * one dedicated command execution routed through its own endpoint\\n* No partial commit on failed plan validation.\\n* The client never submits user-edited ops for apply.\\n\"}]}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":414,"output":3078,"cacheRead":94464,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":97956,"cost":{"input":0.0010350000000000001,"output":0.04617,"cacheRead":0.023615999999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.070821}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1776407364065,"responseId":"resp_0e754b82ab019da10169e1d344fe8c81938243c8124eff1fe2"}}
